#  TurboGAP IR spectrum
#  Fourier transform of the total-dipole autocorrelation function,
#  I(nu) = nu^p * dt * FT[C(tau)], intensity in arbitrary units.
#
#  MD timestep                  =         0.2500 fs
#  MD steps run                 =          12000
#  sampling interval dt         =         0.2500 fs
#  frames in the ensemble       =           7626
#  longest lag transformed      =           3813
#  longest lag sized for        =           3813
#  nu power p                   =         2.0000
#  lag window                   =           hann
#  correlating                  =  mu - <mu>
#  ACF estimator                =  biased, 1/N
#  fitted scale                 =   5.295073E-07
#
#  TRUSTWORTHY RANGE:      420.33  to     3993.10  cm^-1
#
#    Nyquist limit          =     66712.82 cm^-1 = 1/(2 dt).
#      Nothing above it is represented. Power that was there is not
#      absent from this file, it has folded back down into the range
#      below, so read the last 10% up to the Nyquist limit -- above
#      the upper bound quoted above -- as possibly aliased, not signal.
#    resolution             =        34.99 cm^-1 = 1/(n_lag dt).
#      Two bands closer together than this are one band here, and
#      structure narrower than it is the lag window, not the spectrum.
#      Below one resolution element nothing is resolved at all.
#
#    grid written           =       420.33 to     3993.10 cm^-1; the range above is
#      that grid intersected with [resolution, 0.9*Nyquist].
#
#    C(tau) is averaged over n_frames - tau pairs, so the long-lag
#    end is the noisiest part of the transform: fine structure near
#    the resolution limit needs a longer run, not a finer grid.
#
#  wavenumber_cm-1        predicted           experimental
